{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Upon the pure menorah.</b> Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote in the section of <b>ואתה תצוה</b>: there it did not say 'upon the pure menorah' but only ״יערוך אותו אהרן ובניו״, because that section is not the core of the commandment of the lamps — for the meaning of <b>ואתה תצוה</b> is 'you are ultimately to command the children of Israel' — whereas this section is the core of that commandment. Therefore it specifies ״על המנורה הטהורה״, for when it said there (Exodus 27:21) ״יערוך אותו אהרן ובניו״, it could have been understood as upon the menorah or even without a menorah, if it should break or be lost, as was the case when they returned from exile. But now it states explicitly ״על המנורה הטהורה״, because here it comes to clarify the essence of the commandment: that they may kindle only upon a pure menorah. And the rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: ״על המנורה הטהורה״ — upon the purity of the menorah, that one may not support it with magical charms or stones. ״יערוך את הנרות לפני ה׳״ — that one may not prepare them outside and bring them in. ״תמיד״ — even on the Sabbath. ״תמיד״ — even in impurity."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:02.225451714Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}